# Pull the mdev persistent-storage helper into the FIRST-STAGE initramfs.
#
# pmOS's own initramfs mdev.conf (installed by 00-initramfs-base.files as
# /etc/mdev.conf) contains rules like:
#
#     sd[a-z].*   0:0 0660 */lib/mdev/persistent-storage
#
# ...but nothing in mkinitfs's file lists ever copies /lib/mdev/ in. On a
# device whose rootfs lives on UFS that is fatal: every block device that
# appears makes mdev try to exec a helper that is not there
#
#     /lib/mdev/persistent-storage: not found
#
# so /dev/disk/by-uuid/ and /dev/disk/by-partlabel/ are never populated.
# find_root_partition() resolves root BY UUID, finds nothing, falls back to
# scanning for "subpartitions", finds none of those either, and drops to the
# debug shell with "ERROR: failed to mount subpartitions!" — while the disk
# was present and healthy the whole time.
#
# The file itself comes from the mdev-conf package (see depends in APKBUILD).
/lib/mdev/persistent-storage
